  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Armenia Workforce Development</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Armenia):  .Currently in Armenia, there is a mismatch in the labor market between supply and demand. The Workforce Development activity promotes efforts to address the significant labor market gaps and low levels of female and youth labor market participation, including reducing the gap between the skills of the workforce and the needs of employers. It also focuses on improving societal misconceptions about vocational education and employment. The overarching goal of the activity is to improve the soft and technical skills of youth and women and increase their linkages to occupations in key and/or growing sectors by reducing barriers to entry in the labor market. Through training and technical assistance the activity: (1) reduces the gap between the skills of the workforce and the needs of employers; (2) shapes societal perceptions to support effective labor market participation; and (3) improves the operating and enabling legal regulatory environment of labor market development. The principles underlying the strategic and operational approach of the activity include: positive youth development; gender equality; private sector engagement; local ownership and sustainability; and data-driven decision making..The Interim National Security Strategic Guidance seeks to Advance American Interests by renewing partnerships, investing in development assistance to create new markets and mitigate the root causes of instability, and by championing equity and inclusion. The activity also contributes to JSP Goal 2 and Mission Objective 2.1 of the Integrated Country Strategy for Armenia by seeking to advance youth leadership and inclusive economic growth, including through workforce improvements to meet market demands. . .</narrative>
  </description>
